                        "description": "Lesson end time without a timezone offset, in `HH:mm` or `HH:mm:ss` format, for example `17:30` or `17:30:00`. Both forms are accepted on create and update; responses return the stored value. Hours can exceed 23 for an overnight lesson: `25:30:00` means 1:30 am on the day after `date`. When creating a lesson, the latest permitted value is `32:00` or `32:00:00` (8:00 am next day). Matches the supplied timetable time (`HH:mm` or `HH:mm:ss`). A comma-separated list matches any of the times. Comparisons preserve overnight hours such as `25:30`. Operators: `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `eq`, `ne`, `neq`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[endTime][gte]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[endTime]={\"gte\":\"…\"}`.",
