                    {
                        "name": "filter[startDate]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "The order's own billing period start — stored, and one of the three things `PATCH` can change. Not the same as `firstDate`. Matches that calendar date. A comma-separated list matches any of the dates. Operators: `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `eq`, `ne`, `neq`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[startDate][gte]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[startDate]={\"gte\":\"…\"}`.",
