                    {
                        "name": "filter[originalId]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "On an edited note, points at the version it replaced. Editing keeps history rather than overwriting. Exact match. A comma-separated list becomes an `IN (...)` match, and an explicit `null` matches rows where the field is unset. Operators: `eq`, `neq`, `ne`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[originalId][eq]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[originalId]={\"eq\":\"…\"}`.",
