        "/leads/{id}": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "getLeadsId",
                "tags": [
                    "Leads"
                ],
                "summary": "Get one lead",
                "description": "**Why you'll use it**\n\nLoad a single enquiry before calling the family back, or to check what was captured on the form.\n\n**Example queries**\n\n- `/14022?include=center`  \n  One lead with its centre attached.\n\n**Related records you can pull in** (`?include=`)\n\n- `center` — The centre the lead belongs to, as `{id, name}`.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "id",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "description": "Identifier of the record to act on. A record outside the centres your key covers reports `404`, never `403`.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "fields[lead]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Return only these fields, comma separated. `id` is always included whether you ask for it or not. The key is the model's table name, so it is `fields[lead]` for this resource.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "example": "name,fullName,localName"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "include",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Related records to embed in the response, comma separated.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "example": "center"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "withTrashed",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Include soft-deleted records alongside live ones. PAID plan only — a FREE key is silently given the normal, non-deleted result set instead.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "boolean"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "onlyTrashed",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Return only soft-deleted records. PAID plan only — a FREE key is silently given the normal, non-deleted result set instead.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "boolean"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "The requested record.",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "properties": {
                                        "data": {
                                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Lead"
                                        },
                                        "meta": {
                                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Meta"
                                        }
                                    },
                                    "required": [
                                        "data",
                                        "meta"
                                    ]
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "401": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/ValidationFailed"
                    },
                    "429": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"
                    },
                    "500": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/order-items": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "getOrderItems",
                "tags": [
                    "Orders"
                ],
                "summary": "List orders",
                "description": "**Why you'll use it**\n\nBuild a sales report, reconcile revenue by product or teacher, or trace exactly what a payment covered.\n\n**Before you send**\n\nPAID plan only. One behaviour catches people out: **a refund does not delete the line**. Issuing a return reduces the line's own quantity and total, so the row survives. Refunded lines are excluded by default; `filter[refunded]=true` returns only those. That is a different question from `withTrashed`, which is about soft-deleted rows.\n\n**Plan**\n\nPAID plan only. A FREE key gets `403 Order access is not included in the current subscription plan.`.\n\n**Example queries**\n\n- `?filter[billDate][gte]=2026-03-01&filter[billDate][lte]=2026-03-31&include=customer`  \n  A month of sales with the buyer attached.\n- `?filter[type]=C&filter[customerId]=9101`  \n  One student's course purchases.\n- `?filter[refunded]=true&filter[billDate][gte]=2026-01-01`  \n  Refunds this year — invisible without the flag.\n- `?filter[productId][exists]=true&sort=-total`  \n  Product sales, biggest first.\n- `?include=receipt.incomeItems&filter[receiptId]=66104`  \n  What a single receipt paid for, with the payment methods broken out.\n\n**Related records you can pull in** (`?include=`)\n\n- `customer` — Who bought it, as `{id, name, number}`.\n- `staff` — Who sold it, as `{id, name}`.\n- `invoice` — The invoice it was billed on, summarised.\n- `receipt` — The receipt it was paid on, summarised. Its `incomeItems` are only filled in if you ask for `receipt.incomeItems`.\n- `receipt.incomeItems` — The individual payments on that receipt — cash, card, credit. Ask for this rather than plain `receipt` when you need the payment breakdown, otherwise it comes back empty.\n- `fee` — The fee it was priced from, as `{id, name}`.\n- `product` — The product sold, as `{id, name}`.\n- `tax` — The tax applied, as `{id, name, rate}`.\n- `center` — The centre, as `{id, name}`.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "page",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Page number, starting at 1. How deep you may page is capped by your plan — 5 pages on FREE and 200 on PAID, independent of page size. Going past the cap is a `422`, not an empty page.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "default": 1
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "pageSize",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Records per page. Defaults to 50, with a hard ceiling of 500 and a plan ceiling of 50 on FREE / 500 on PAID. Asking for more than your plan allows returns `422` — it is never silently clamped.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "default": 50
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "perPage",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Alias for `pageSize`. If both are sent, `pageSize` wins.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "sort",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Sort by one or more fields, comma separated. Prefix a field with `-` to sort descending (`sort=-created,name`). Sorting by anything outside the list below is rejected.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "x-allowed-fields": [
                                "id",
                                "centerId",
                                "invoiceId",
                                "receiptId",
                                "customerId",
                                "staffId",
                                "type",
                                "feeId",
                                "productId",
                                "category",
                                "name",
                                "detail",
                                "remark",
                                "regular",
                                "extended",
                                "frequency",
                                "price",
                                "quantity",
                                "startDate",
                                "endDate",
                                "discount",
                                "percent",
                                "rawDiscount",
                                "rawPercent",
                                "rewardSchemeId",
                                "total",
                                "paid",
                                "totalPreTax",
                                "taxRate",
                                "taxId",
                                "scheduled",
                                "quota",
                                "quotaUnit",
                                "paidQuota",
                                "billDate",
                                "feeSpec",
                                "created",
                                "updated",
                                "deleted"
                            ]
                        },
                        "example": "-created"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "fields[order_item]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Return only these fields, comma separated. `id` is always included whether you ask for it or not. The key is the model's table name, so it is `fields[order_item]` for this resource.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "example": "centerId,invoiceId,receiptId"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "include",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Related records to embed in the response, comma separated.",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "example": "customer,staff"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "filter[billDate]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Matches that calendar date. A comma-separated list matches any of the dates. Operators: `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `eq`, `ne`, `neq`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[billDate][gte]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[billDate]={\"gte\":\"…\"}`.",
                        "schema": {
                            "oneOf": [
                                {
                                    "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "additionalProperties": true,
                                    "x-operators": [
                                        "gt",
                                        "gte",
                                        "lt",
                                        "lte",
                                        "eq",
                                        "ne",
                                        "neq",
                                        "in",
                                        "nin",
                                        "exists"
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "filter[category]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Exact match. A comma-separated list becomes an `IN (...)` match, and an explicit `null` matches rows where the field is unset. Operators: `eq`, `neq`, `ne`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[category][eq]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[category]={\"eq\":\"…\"}`.",
                        "schema": {
                            "oneOf": [
                                {
                                    "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "additionalProperties": true,
                                    "x-operators": [
                                        "eq",
                                        "neq",
                                        "ne",
                                        "in",
                                        "nin",
                                        "exists"
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "filter[centerId]",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Exact match. A comma-separated list becomes an `IN (...)` match, and an explicit `null` matches rows where the field is unset. Operators: `eq`, `neq`, `ne`, `in`, `nin`, `exists` — e.g. `filter[centerId][eq]=…`, or the JSON form `filter[centerId]={\"eq\":\"…\"}`.",
                        "schema": {
                            "oneOf": [
                                {
                                    "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "additionalProperties": true,
                                    "x-operators": [
                                        "eq",
                                        "neq",
                                        "ne",
                                        "in",
                                        "nin",
                                        "exists"
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    },
